thing.ts:3`-`10`). Direct repro: `cleanPrompt(\\\"fix this\\\\n```ts\\\\nconst  i = 1;\\\\n\\\\n\\\\treturn  i;\\\\n```\\\\nthanks\\\")` returned `\\\"fix this\\\\n```ts\\\\nconst I = 1;\\\\n\\\\nreturn I;\\\\n```\\\\nthanks\\\"`, changing spaces, tab indentation, and `i` inside the fenced block. The existing fenced test uses `const value = 1;` and a provider stub that returns a fixed preserved block (`packages/lhc/test/smoothing-recovery.test.ts:168`-`193`), so it does not prove byte-identical preservation for fenced content affected by deterministic cleaning.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/smoothing.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/handlers.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/smoothing-recovery.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.3\",\"TC-1.3a\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-01-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Deterministic cleaning mutates fenced code before inference\",\"evidence\":\"AC-1.3/TC-1.3a requires fenced code to remain unchanged through inference smoothing. `smoothPromptHandler` computes `cleaned = cleanPrompt(text)` and sends that value to `provider.smoothPrompt` (`packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/handlers.ts:83`, `packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/handlers.ts:104`). `cleanPrompt` applies whitespace and casing replacements to the whole prompt (`packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/smoothing.ts:3`-`10`). Direct repro: `cleanPrompt(\\\"fix this\\\\n```ts\\\\nconst  i = 1;\\\\n\\\\n\\\\treturn  i;\\\\n```\\\\nthanks\\\")` returned `\\\"fix this\\\\n```ts\\\\nconst I = 1;\\\\n\\\\nreturn I;\\\\n```\\\\nthanks\\\"`, changing spaces, tab indentation, and `i` inside the fenced block. The existing fenced test uses `const value = 1;` and a provider stub that returns a fixed preserved block (`packages/lhc/test/smoothing-recovery.test.ts:168`-`193`), so it does not prove byte-identical preservation for fenced content affected by deterministic cleaning.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/smoothing.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/handlers.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/smoothing-recovery.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.3\",\"TC-1.3a\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true}],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"AC-1.1 / TC-1.1a, TC-1.1b: deterministic cleaning runs before provider work and over-cap prompts still store cleaned output.\",\"AC-1.2 / TC-1.2a, TC-1.2b: under-cap smoothing invokes `smoothPrompt`; over-cap smoothing stores deterministic output with no provider call.\",\"AC-1.4 / TC-1.4a, TC-1.4b: deterministic-only and inference-success smoothing land `ready`; no skipped/degraded state was found.\",\"AC-1.5 / TC-1.5a, TC-1.5b: retryable provider failure leaves `smoothed_prompt` pending and queued; turn composition consumes deterministic floor.\",\"AC-1.6 / TC-1.6a: intake queues `prompt_smoothing` and provider capture remains empty during intake.\",\"AC-1.7 / TC-1.7a, TC-1.7b: exhausted smoothing failure lands `failed` with reason; turn composition consumes deterministic floor.\"],\"unverified\":[\"AC-1.3 / TC-1.3a: fenced-code byte preservation is contradicted by `cleanPrompt` mutating fenced content before inference.\"]},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"cd packages/lhc && pnpm exec vitest run test/smoothing-recovery.test.ts\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"cd packages/lhc && pnpm run verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"cd packages/lhc && pnpm run verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"}],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"`smoothPromptHandler` sends globally cleaned text to the provider, so under-cap production smoothing can mutate fenced code before the `smoothing-v1` prompt instruction has any chance to preserve it.\"],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"revise\",\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"openQuestions\":[],\"additionalObservations\":[\"No material fake-adapter,